<!-- FEVERWOOD_FLORA_ROSTER_1 build. Authority:
     design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/fever_wood_flora_roster_2026-09-23.md
     — 18 RM_-tier invented plants, organised by height above the water
     (3 towers, 8 crown, 4 pool margin, 3 ground). Replaces the 3 AB_*
     donor rows (`AB_KeeningCordax`/`AB_Iashiphus`/`AB_Gomphoeria`) that
     shipped inline on RM_FeverWood.xml — cut per the roster's own §6
     disposition table. RM_GiantLeaf (already RM_-tier, invented, not a
     donor placeholder) is untouched; it was never one of the rows this
     roster replaces. The 3 genuine canon Star Wars rows
     (Plant_HydenockTree_Wild/Plant_JoganTree_Wild/Plant_Chakroot_Wild)
     already ride the Utinni patch layer (WildAnimals_FeverWood.xml) per
     Q11a and are untouched by this build — they are additive canon
     flavour, kept at existing low commonality, not part of the 18.

     🔴 Every commonality and growDays value below is an ENGINEERING
     DEFAULT, not an owner ruling — the roster doc's own §8 says outright
     "every number here is a slot, not a value." Same disclosure shape as
     RUT_BoughSoil.xml's fertility figure. Flag for live tuning.

     ⛔ No row here falls, is fellable, or carries RM_FellableTreeExtension/
     RM_CompCrackFall — the item's own "no row falls" ruling (owner,
     verbatim: mine right through, nothing here can fall). All 18 use
     ParentName="PlantBase", never a Tree parent, so no auto-fell job is
     generated.

     CROWN LAYER FERTILITY GATING: the 8 crown rows (Plennith/Ossagrel/
     Cistrel/Maulith/Verrow/Nubrith/Halquin/Ammeth) set fertilityMin 1.0 —
     high enough that ordinary ground (measured Soil fertility 1.0 at the
     margin, this biome's Soil/SoilRich terrainsByFertility split at 0.9)
     does not reliably clear it, while RUT_BoughSoil (fertility 1.4,
     FEVERWOOD_BOUGH_SOIL_TERRAIN_1, built+deployed this session, offline-
     verified, live bough-soil-paints-and-plants-root check still owed) and
     any natural SoilRich comfortably do. This is the same "no new C#, gate
     on the existing fertility field" mechanism that item's own header
     names as the fitting shape — not a new dependency edge. It is looser
     than "only on RUT_BoughSoil" (any natural SoilRich patch qualifies
     too), an accepted engineering looseness, not an owner ruling.

     ART: RM_Ossagrel ships REAL finished art, copied from
     infrastructure/artpipe/_artsrc/feverwood_plant_ossagrel/ (validated
     PASS, MEASURED 256x256 RGBA) — found by searching artpipe/done before
     queuing anything, per the item's own "before queueing any art"
     section. RM_Thulvane/RM_Skethral/RM_Verrow/RM_Tullick already have
     PENDING artpipe jobs (also found by that search, tagged
     FEVERWOOD_RM_MOD_BUILD_1, generated-but-validated-fail, awaiting a
     daemon retry) — not re-queued here. The other 13 rows get a genuine
     flat-color placeholder PNG (same idiom as RM_FeverWood.png/
     RUT_FeverTrunkHeartwood.png: just enough to load, not a regen, not an
     artpipe job) and a fresh queue entry filed by this build (see
     infrastructure/artpipe/pending/feverwood_plant_<name>.json,
     rimflow_item_id=FEVERWOOD_FLORA_ROSTER_1). -->
<Defs>

  <!-- ===================== THE GIANTS — 3 towers, none falls =====================
       Rare, huge-canvas flavour trees distinct from the mineable body
       (RUT_FeverTrunkHeartwood/RUT_FeverTrunkCore, spawned separately by
       RM_LivingBoleBiomeExtension's own genstep). These are ordinary
       wildPlants entries at very low commonality — matching the 1~2
       boles per map the biome extension already spawns — not fellable,
       not mineable, not wired into that extension's spawn table. Wiring
       a per-species heartwood choice into RM_LivingBoleBiomeExtension's
       C# is a follow-on, out of this item's own def-authoring scope. -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Thulvane</defName>
    <label>thulvane</label>
    <description>A colossal fused column of a tree, its base so broad it reads as several trunks grown together, rising past sight so its crown is simply a permanent green ceiling. Bark in wet vertical plates, black in the grooves, permanently damp. The biome's structural unit — the ceiling, the interlock that keeps anything from falling, and the body colonists mine rooms into.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>160</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Thulvane/RM_Thulvane_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.3, 0.5, 0.3)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>50</pathCost>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.5</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.3</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>40</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <visualSizeRange>2.6~3.5</visualSizeRange>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>3</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>4</wildClusterWeight>
      <purpose>None</purpose>
      <interferesWithRoof>true</interferesWithRoof>
      <blockAdjacentSow>true</blockAdjacentSow>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Skethral</defName>
    <label>skethral</label>
    <description>Shorter and wider than a thulvane, and visibly reaching: its heavy limbs grow horizontally toward its neighbours and fuse where they meet, so two skethrals read as one arch. Bark smooth and pale at the joins, scarred where limbs have knitted. This is the tree that grows the boughway roads — the in-fiction reason the crown is interlocked at all.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>140</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Skethral/RM_Skethral_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.3, 0.4, 0.3)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>40</pathCost>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.5</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.3</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>35</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <visualSizeRange>2.2~3.0</visualSizeRange>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>3</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>5</wildClusterWeight>
      <purpose>None</purpose>
      <interferesWithRoof>true</interferesWithRoof>
      <blockAdjacentSow>true</blockAdjacentSow>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Varnoth</defName>
    <label>varnoth</label>
    <description>Rooted in a mirror pool itself, on a tripod of prop-roots clear of the surface, its trunk leaning out over the water. Its lower bark is stained and polished to a wet black by the pool. Nothing grows beneath it. Its timber is the best in the biome — and it stands inside the reach, so reward and hazard are the same object.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>110</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Varnoth/RM_Varnoth_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.25, 0.4, 0.25)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>30</pathCost>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.2</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.2</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>30</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <harvestYield>60</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>900</harvestWork>
      <harvestedThingDef>WoodLog</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <visualSizeRange>1.8~2.5</visualSizeRange>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>2</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>3</wildClusterWeight>
      <purpose>None</purpose>
      <interferesWithRoof>true</interferesWithRoof>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ===================== THE CROWN — 8 plants, on bough-soil ===================== -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Plennith</defName>
    <label>plennith</label>
    <description>A dense low mat of overlapping grey-green scales lying directly along bark and bough, thickening into a spongy bed that visibly holds silt and rot. Reads as a surface, never as a plant. This is what makes the bough-soil — the crown's fertility is biological, not geological, and where plennith has run, other things can grow.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Plennith/RM_Plennith_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>2</pathCost>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>1.0</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.6</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>6</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <visualSizeRange>0.8~1.1</visualSizeRange>
      <wildOrder>3</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>8</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>60</wildClusterWeight>
      <purpose>None</purpose>
      <interferesWithRoof>false</interferesWithRoof>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Ossagrel</defName>
    <label>ossagrel</label>
    <description>A thick segmented cane clamped along a bough, each joint swollen and split, weeping clear syrup that glazes and crusts below it. The whole plant looks over-full, and the bark under it is sugared and crawling. The host the crown's sap-suckers drink from, and the sugar line for stills and nectar-liquor.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Ossagrel/RM_Ossagrel_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>4</pathCost>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>1.0</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.6</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>14</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <harvestYield>10</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>300</harvestWork>
      <harvestedThingDef>RM_OssagrelSap</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <visualSizeRange>0.9~1.4</visualSizeRange>
      <wildOrder>2</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>4</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>25</wildClusterWeight>
      <purpose>Food</purpose>
      <interferesWithRoof>false</interferesWithRoof>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_OssagrelSap</defName>
    <label>ossagrel sap</label>
    <description>Sugar-thick syrup wept from ossagrel canes. Distills into a rough liquor or ferments into nectar; the crown's own sap-suckers drink it straight from the plant.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_OssagrelSap/RM_OssagrelSap</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
