    <description>One stiff flat fan of fused leaf held in a single plane from a short base, so it reads as a panel from one side and a line edge-on — the only plant here whose silhouette changes with facing. Waxy, rain-shedding, pale underneath. Roofing and decking; the cheapest building material in the biome, cut but never felled.</description>
